5. Core Business Requirements
Area	Requirement
Employee Profile	Capture employee, role, grade, department, manager, primary capability and profile completeness.
Skill Profile	Allow employees to add skills, experience, last-used date, proficiency and supporting evidence.
Assessment	Enable self-assessment followed by manager, project, technical, certification-based or panel assessment.
Proficiency Model	Use five levels: 1 Awareness, 2 Foundation, 3 Practitioner, 4 Advanced and 5 Expert.
Certification	Track provider, related skill, issue date, expiry date, certificate, status and verification.
Learning	Maintain a training catalogue, recommendations, enrolment, completion, score and evidence.
Project Demand	Capture project skills, required proficiency, headcount, priority and requirement period.
Matching	Compare project demand with approved employee skills and show transparent match factors.
Analytics	Provide capability, skill-gap, certification, workforce and future-demand dashboards.
6. Key Screens
•	Home Dashboard: personal capability summary, pending actions and development opportunities.
•	My Profile and My Skills: employee information, skills, evidence, assessment status and proficiency.
•	Assessment: manager review, comments, approval or rejection.
•	Manager Dashboard: team skill matrix, assessment progress, gaps, expiry and training needs.
•	Skill Gap and Project Matching: demand versus supply and suitable resource results.
•	Certification Dashboard and Admin: credential tracking, taxonomy, roles and configuration.
7. Automation and Security
Area	Initial Requirement
Power Automate	New employee profile, skill assessment, assessment approval, 90/60/30-day certification reminders, incomplete-profile reminders, training recommendations, project gap calculation and periodic skill review.
Security	Microsoft Entra ID authentication with role-based access for Employee, Manager, Capability Manager, Project Manager and Administrator.
Data Access	Employees see their own records; managers see authorised teams; capability managers see organisational capability; administrators manage configuration.
Governance	Use approved taxonomies, evidence-based assessments, audit history, least privilege and controlled master-data changes.
8. Recommended Phased Delivery
Phase	Scope
Phase 1 | MVP	Employees, Skills, Employee Skills and Assessments; Employee and Manager Power Apps; skill matrix and basic dashboard.
Phase 2	Certifications, Training, Power Automate workflows, reminders and notifications.
Phase 3	Projects, skill requirements, resource matching and skill-gap analytics.
Phase 4	Power BI, AI-assisted skill extraction, profile parsing, advanced matching and forecasting.
9. Discussion Points and Next Step
Confirm data source, user volume, taxonomy ownership, assessment governance, manager visibility, privacy rules, matching logic, reporting scope and Dataverse migration thresholds. After discussion, prepare the detailed developer build specification.

